    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "I collected evidence for all four CLIs. Every model and default the bundled catalogue uses for gemini, qwen, agent and opencode is out of date. I only ran `--help`, `--version`, `opencode models` and read the installed code; no paid APIs were called. The four evidence files are in `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791364120785/docs/case-studies/issue-2591/data/cli-model-catalogues/`, each under 150 lines.\n\n**Gemini CLI 0.62.0** (`gemini-0.62.0-aliases.txt`, source is the bundle's `chunk-2DHAEQE2.js`)\n- **Default:** `auto` (`gemini-CGCV5XPN.js:8439`: `const defaultModel = GEMINI_MODEL_ALIAS_AUTO`).\n- **How the aliases resolve** (`modelIdResolutions`):\n  - `auto` and `pro` → `gemini-3-pro-preview`, or `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` once Gemini 3.1 is enabled for the account (`-customtools` variant with an API key). Without preview access they fall back to `gemini-2.5-pro`.\n  - `flash` → `gemini-3-flash-preview`. With the newest flash enabled it is `gemini-3.8-flash`; without preview access it is `gemini-3.5-flash`.\n  - `flash-lite` → `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, or `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` with the newest flash-lite enabled.\n  - Hidden aliases: `auto-gemini-3` and `auto-gemini-2.5` (the latter → `gemini-2.5-pro`).\n- **Current concrete models:** `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` (and `-customtools`), `gemini-3-pro-preview`, `gemini-3-flash-preview`, `gemini-3.5-flash`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `gemini-3-flash`, `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, `gemini-3.5-flash-lite`, `gemini-2.5-pro`, `gemma-4-31b-it`, `gemma-4-26b-a4b-it`.\n- **`gemini-2.5-flash` and `gemini-2.5-flash-lite` are being dropped.** They are not in `VALID_GEMINI_MODELS`. Requesting `gemini-2.5-flash` is redirected to 3.8-flash when the newest flash is enabled.\n- **The CLI's own docs are stale:** `docs/cli/cli-reference.md` still says flash → 2.5-flash. Our catalogue comment cites that page.\n- **Obsolete in our catalogue:** `flash`, `gemini`, `gemini-flash` and `2.5-flash` → `gemini-2.5-flash`; `lite`, `flash-lite` and `2.5-lite` → `gemini-2.5-flash-lite`; `pro` and `gemini-pro` → `gemini-2.5-pro` (only the fallback now). Our default `gemini: 'flash'` therefore pins 2.5-flash.\n- **Recommended:**\n  - Pass `pro`, `flash` and `flash-lite` through to the CLI unchanged, as `auto` already is, so the CLI picks the right model per account.\n  - Add `3.1-pro` / `gemini-3.1-pro-preview`, `3.5-flash`, `3.8-flash`, `3.1-flash-lite`, `3.5-flash-lite` and `auto-gemini-3`.\n  - Keep the 2.5 IDs only as legacy pins.\n  - Make the default `auto`, or at least `flash` passed through.\n\n**Qwen Code 0.24.7** (`qwen-0.24.7-models.txt`)\n- **The Qwen OAuth free tier is gone:** \"Qwen OAuth free tier was discontinued on 2026-04-15. Run /auth to switch to Coding Plan, OpenRouter…\" (`chunk-W6JL5XM3.js`).\n- **Defaults:** `DEFAULT_QWEN_MODEL=\"coder-model\"` for qwen-oauth, which is the only allowed OAuth model (\"Qwen 3.7 Max\"). For API-key auth the default is `MAINLINE_CODER_MODEL=\"qwen3.7-max\"`.\n- **Preset model lists:**\n  - Token Plan / Standard API key: `qwen3.8-max`, `qwen3.8-max-0902`, `qwen3.8-max-preview`, `qwen3.8-flash`, `qwen3.7-max`, `qwen3.7-plus`, `qwen3.6-plus`, `qwen3.6-flash`, plus deepseek, kimi and glm models.\n  - Coding Plan (`MODELSTUDIO_MODELS`): `qwen3.5-plus`, `qwen3.6-plus`, `qwen3.7-plus`, `qwen3-coder-plus`, `qwen3-coder-next`, `qwen3-max-2026-01-23`, and others.\n- **Obsolete in our catalogue:**\n  - Default `qwen3-coder-plus`, plus `qwen`, `qwen-coder` and `qwen3` all pointing at it. It survives only in the Coding Plan preset.\n  - `qwen3-coder-flash` and `qwen3-coder` appear only in a token-limit rule and settings examples.\n  - `qwen3.6-coder-plus` does not appear anywhere in the bundle.\n- **Recommended:**\n  - Point `qwen`, `qwen-coder` and `qwen3` at the latest model (`qwen3.7-max` / `coder-model`), and change the default to `qwen3.7-max`.\n  - Add `coder-model`, `max` → `qwen3.8-max`, `plus` → `qwen3.7-plus`, `flash` → `qwen3.8-flash`, and the concrete 3.7/3.8 IDs.\n  - Drop `qwen3.6-coder-plus`.\n\n**agent 0.26.11** (`agent-0.26.11-models.txt`)\n- **There is no `models` subcommand.** The free list is fetched live from `opencode.ai/zen/v1/models`, with hardcoded fallbacks in `src/provider/opencode-zen.ts`.\n- **Default:** `opencode/minimax-m2.5-free` (`src/config/defaults.ts`, also shown by `--help`). Our default is `nemotron-3-super-free`, which no longer matches.\n- **The agent's own built-in fallbacks are dead.** The local models.dev snapshot (`~/.cache/opencode/models.json`) marks these as deprecated: `minimax-m2.5-free`, `nemotron-3-super-free`, `hy3-preview-free`, `ling-2.6-flash-free`, `grok-code`. `gpt-5-nano` is now paid.\n- **Kilo:** none of the agent's Kilo free IDs are in the snapshot (`z-ai/glm-5:free`, `glm-4.5-air:free`, `minimax-m2.5:free`, `trinity-large-preview:free`, `deepseek-r1-0528:free`, `giga-potato`). That snapshot is third-party data, not the live Kilo API.\n- **Obsolete in our `agentModels`:**\n  - All `opencode/*` free entries except `big-pickle`: grok and grok-code, `gpt-5-nano`, minimax, nemotron-3-super, plus the entries already marked deprecated.\n  - All `kilo/*` entries.\n  - The premium targets `anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet`, `claude-3-5-haiku`, `claude-3-opus` and `google/gemini-3-pro`, none of which are in the snapshot.\n- **Missing:** the 11 currently free Zen models listed under OpenCode below. Paid snapshot IDs (unverified for the agent itself) include `opencode/claude-sonnet-5-5`, `claude-opus-5-5`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `gpt-6.1-sol`, `grok-4.7`, `glm-5.3`, `kimi-k3`, `minimax-m3` and `qwen3.8-max`.\n- **Recommended:**\n  - Add the current free models.\n  - Move the dead ones to a deprecated block.\n  - Map `sonnet`/`opus`/`haiku` to current Claude IDs (`opencode/claude-sonnet-5-5` etc.).\n  - Pick a current free model as the default (`big-pickle` or `nemotron-3-ultra-free`). Since the agent upstream is also stale, this is worth raising there.\n\n**OpenCode 1.18.34** (`opencode-1.18.34-models.txt`)\n- **`opencode models` lists 11 models, three more than the 8 in your brief:** `opencode/big-pickle`, `exo-free`, `fledge-alpha-free`, `ling-3.0-flash-fin-free`, `ling-3.1-flash-free`, `longcat-2.5-preview-free`, `mimo-v2.6-flash-free`, `muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free`, `nemotron-3-ultra-free`, `nemotron-3.5-lightning-free`, `space-bunny-free`. The new ones are `exo-free`, `fledge-alpha-free` and `ling-3.1-flash-free`.\n- **Default:** the binary's selection order is config → most recently used model → priority list `[\"gpt-5\",\"claude-sonnet-4\",\"big-pickle\",\"gemini-3-pro\"]`. With only free models available that gives `opencode/big-pickle`.\n- **Obsolete in our `opencodeModels`:**\n  - Default `grok-code-fast-1` and every grok alias → `opencode/grok-code`, which is deprecated.\n  - `claude`/`sonnet` → `anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet`, `opus` → `claude-3-opus`, and `gemini` → `google/gemini-pro` are all missing from the snapshot.\n  - `gpt4` is deprecated.\n- **Recommended:**\n  - Change the default to `big-pickle`.\n  - Add the free short names and `big-pickle`.\n  - Map `sonnet` → `anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5`, `opus` → `claude-opus-5-5`, `gemini` → `google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview`, or the `opencode/*` equivalents.\n\n**Outside the four CLIs:** the snapshot also lists `claude-sonnet-5-5` (released 2026-09-28) under the anthropic and opencode providers. `claudeModels` has no `sonnet-5-5` entry and `sonnet` still points at `claude-sonnet-5`.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The snapshot is the local models.dev cache from 2026-10-07 09:18, used offline. \"Deprecated\" and \"missing\" come from that data, not from live API calls.\n- Some Gemini resolutions depend on per-account flags (preview access, newest flash, Gemini 3.1). That is why passing the aliases through is safer than pinning them."
      }
