        "type": "text",
        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591, titled \"We must support all obvious aliases for latest versions of models\". Work only on branch `issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2` in /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791364120785, and update the existing PR #2592 instead of creating a new one.\n\n   The issue asks for the following:\n   - **Bare family aliases.** In the screenshot, `/codex https://github.com/link-assistant/calculator/issues/227 —think high —model astra` fails with `Unrecognized model: \"astra\"`, `Did you mean: \"terra\"?` and then lists about 60 models. `astra` should resolve to the latest `gpt-6-astra`, or whatever the latest Astra is at that moment.\n   - **Dynamic aliases.** New aliases should be picked up from new model names without code changes.\n   - **Full model support.** Every available model should be supported to its full potential.\n   - **Real model lists.** The \"Available models\" list must reflect what is actually available in Codex, Claude and the other harnesses, so obsolete models are not shown.\n   - **Case study.** Download all related logs and data into `./docs/case-studies/issue-2591`. Write a deep case study covering:\n     - a timeline,\n     - every requirement in the issue,\n     - root causes,\n     - proposed solutions and plans,\n     - existing components or libraries that help,\n     - additional facts found online.\n   - **Debug output.** If the data is not enough to find the root cause, add debug or verbose output.\n   - **Upstream reports.** If another repository is involved, report issues there with reproducible examples, workarounds and suggested fixes.\n   - **Apply everywhere.** Fix every place in the codebase where the problem occurs.\n   - **Single PR.** Do everything in this one PR.\n\n   Standard solver guidelines also apply:\n   - Write a reproducing test first.\n   - Keep experiment scripts in ./experiments and examples in ./examples.\n   - Commit atomic steps and push only to this branch.\n   - Run local checks before committing (eslint, prettier, tests).\n   - Add a changeset or version bump if the repo uses one (it uses `.changeset/*.md`).\n   - Update the PR title and description with `gh pr edit 2592`, then run `gh pr ready 2592`.\n   - Check CI.\n   - Do not remove existing features without being asked.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Model catalogue modules.** The bundled catalogue is `src/models/catalog.mjs`. Mapping and validation live in `src/models/index.mjs`, and the live catalogue is in `src/model-catalogue.lib.mjs` (issue #2202, which also has sources, fetch and render modules).\n   - **Codex family aliases (issue #2043).** `getLatestCodexGenerationAliases` only promotes `sol`/`terra`/`luna` when one generation has all three. GPT-6 has sol, luna and astra but no terra, so today `sol` → `gpt-5.6-sol` and `luna` → `gpt-5.6-luna` (stale), and `astra` is undefined.\n   - **Prefixed variants.** `CODEX_MODEL_VARIANTS` generates `openai/` and `openai.` variants of every model. These flood the error listing.\n   - **Codex runtime discovery.**\n     - `getInstalledCodexModels()` runs `codex debug models`, takes about 0.17s, and is cached per process forever.\n     - `resolveRuntimeDefaultModel` picks the newest Sol.\n     - `validateRuntimeModelName` (async) runs static validation first, then an exact live match, then provider-shaped pass-through.\n   - **Execution-time mapping is static.** `src/codex.options.lib.mjs` has `mapModelToId = model => CODEX_MODEL_VARIANTS[model] || model`, used in codex.lib.mjs at lines 447, 533 and 658. Claude uses `mapModelToId` in `src/claude.model-utils.lib.mjs`, backed by CLAUDE_MODELS, with `ROLLING_CLAUDE_ALIASES = {opus, sonnet, haiku}` preserved for direct runs. Any dynamic alias therefore also has to be resolved at execution time.\n   - **Real Codex catalogue** (`codex debug models`, codex-cli 0.160.0, 2026-10-07):\n\n     | Model | Visibility | Description | Upgrade target |\n     |---|---|---|---|\n     | gpt-6-astra | list | Frontier intelligence | — |\n     | gpt-6.1-sol | list | Latest workhorse | — |\n     | gpt-6-sol | list | Previous generation workhorse | — |\n     | gpt-6-luna | list | Fast and affordable | — |\n     | gpt-5.6-sol | list | — | gpt-6-sol |\n     | gpt-5.6-terra | list | — | gpt-6-sol |\n     | gpt-5.6-luna | list | — | gpt-6-luna |\n     | gpt-daybreak-blue-latest | hide | — | — |\n     | gpt-daybreak-red-latest | hide | — | — |\n     | gpt-5.5 | list | Legacy | gpt-6-sol |\n     | codex-auto-review | hide | — | — |\n\n     Obsolete bundled entries:\n     - gpt-reserve\n     - gpt-5 and gpt5\n     - gpt-5.5-mini and gpt-5.5-nano\n     - gpt-5.6-cyber\n     - gpt-5.4, gpt-5.4-mini and gpt-5.4-nano\n     - gpt-5.2 and gpt-5.2-codex\n     - gpt-5.3-codex and gpt-5.3-codex-spark\n     - gpt-5.1-codex-max\n     - o3-mini\n     - gpt-4/gpt4 and gpt-4o/gpt4o\n   - **Claude Code 2.1.292 binary:**\n     - Alias list: `[\"sonnet\",\"opus\",\"haiku\",\"fable\",\"best\",\"sonnet[1m]\",\"opus[1m]\",\"fable[1m]\",\"opusplan\"]`.\n     - Alias resolution: opus → claude-opus-5-5, sonnet → claude-sonnet-5-5, haiku → claude-haiku-4-5, fable → claude-fable-5-1, best → fable.\n     - Known IDs include `claude-sonnet-5-5`, which is missing from our catalogue, plus `claude-mythos-5` and `claude-mythos-5-1`.\n     - Gaps in our catalogue: no `mythos` alias, no `best`, no `sonnet-5-5`, and opus/sonnet still map to claude-opus-5 and claude-sonnet-5.\n   - **OpenCode 1.18.34.** `opencode models` lists only these free models:\n     - opencode/big-pickle\n     - ling-3.0-flash-fin-free\n     - longcat-2.5-preview-free\n     - mimo-v2.6-flash-free\n     - muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free\n     - nemotron-3-ultra-free\n     - nemotron-3.5-lightning-free\n     