{
  "type": "user",
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591, \"We must support all obvious aliases for latest versions of models\". Work in /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791364120785, only on branch `issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2`, and update the existing PR #2592 rather than opening a new one.\n\n   What the issue asks for:\n   - **Bare family aliases.** In the screenshot, `/codex ... --model astra` fails with `Unrecognized model: \"astra\"`, `Did you mean: \"terra\"?` and a list of about 60 models. `astra` must resolve to the latest GPT Astra.\n   - **Dynamic aliases.** Aliases should be derived from new model names without code changes.\n   - **Full model support.** Every available model should be supported to its full potential.\n   - **Real model lists.** \"Available models\" must reflect what Codex, Claude and the other CLIs actually offer today, without obsolete entries.\n   - **Case study.** Collect logs and data under `./docs/case-studies/issue-2591` and write a deep case study:\n     - timeline\n     - requirements\n     - root causes\n     - solutions\n     - existing libraries\n     - online research\n   - **Debug output.** Add debug output if it is needed to find the cause.\n   - **Upstream reports.** File issues in other repositories where relevant, with reproductions, workarounds and suggested fixes.\n   - **Apply everywhere.** Fix every place in the codebase where the problem occurs.\n   - **Single PR.** Do all of this in one PR.\n\n   Standard solver guidelines:\n   - Write a reproducing test first.\n   - Keep scripts in ./experiments and ./examples.\n   - Make atomic commits and push only to this branch.\n   - Run eslint, prettier and the tests before committing.\n   - Add a changeset in `.changeset/*.md`.\n   - Update the PR with `gh pr edit 2592`, then run `gh pr ready 2592`.\n   - Check CI.\n   - Do not remove existing features.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Leaf module `src/models/aliases.mjs`** (no imports):\n     - `deriveCodexFamilyAliases`: `^gpt-(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)*)-([a-z]+)$` gives each family its own newest version. `gpt-<name>-latest` gives the alias `<name>`.\n     - `deriveClaudeFamilyAliases`: `^claude-([a-z]+)-(\\d+(?:-\\d+)?)$` gives `family-ver`, the dotted forms `family-5.5` and `claude-family-5.5`, and `family` → newest version.\n     - `listClaudeFamilies`, `deriveFamilyAliasesForTool`, `compareNumericVersions`.\n     - Runtime alias registry: `registerRuntimeModelAlias(tool, alias, modelId)`, `getRuntimeModelAlias`, `clearRuntimeModelAliases`.\n   - **Codex catalogue split:**\n     - `currentCodexModels`: the 11 IDs from `codex debug models`, codex-cli 0.160.0.\n     - `HIDDEN_CODEX_MODEL_IDS`: the daybreak models and codex-auto-review.\n     - `legacyCodexModels`: still accepted, but not listed.\n     - `CODEX_FAMILY_ALIASES` = {astra: gpt-6-astra, sol: gpt-6.1-sol, luna: gpt-6-luna, terra: gpt-5.6-terra, daybreak-blue, daybreak-red}.\n     - `getLatestCodexGenerationAliases` now delegates to `deriveCodexFamilyAliases(currentCodexModels)`.\n     - `CODEX_MODELS = { ...CODEX_MODEL_VARIANTS }`.\n     - The redundant explicit `openai.*` entries were removed; variants are generated.\n   - **Claude:**\n     - opus → claude-opus-5-5 and sonnet → claude-sonnet-5-5, matching Claude Code 2.1.292's `latest_per_family`.\n     - Added `best` → claude-fable-5-1, `sonnet-5-5`, `claude-sonnet-5-5`, plus derived `mythos` and dotted aliases. Explicit entries take precedence.\n     - `LEGACY_CLAUDE_MODEL_ALIASES = ['haiku-3','haiku-3-5']` are hidden from listings.\n   - **Runtime validation:**\n     - Family alias candidates (codex: keys of CODEX_FAMILY_ALIASES with the openai prefix stripped; claude: names from `listClaudeFamilies`) are resolved against the live catalogue and recorded in the registry.\n     - Claude shorthand such as `opus-6` expands to `claude-opus-6` when the family is known.\n     - When the Codex CLI answers, the error message lists that CLI's visible models plus aliases.\n     - A warning is attached when the chosen model is not in the installed Codex catalogue.\n     - The `codex debug models` cache now has a TTL of 1h by default, overridable with `HIVE_MIND_CODEX_MODELS_CACHE_TTL_MS`.\n   - **Research findings** (saved in `docs/case-studies/issue-2591/data/cli-model-catalogues/`):\n\n     | CLI | Default | Notable findings |\n     |---|---|---|\n     | Gemini CLI 0.62.0 | `auto` | flash → gemini-3-flash-preview or 3.8/3.5-flash; pro → 3/3.1-pro-preview; 2.5-flash and 2.5-flash-lite are being dropped; our catalogue pins 2.5 |\n     | Qwen 0.24.7 | coder-model / qwen3.7-max | OAuth free tier ended 2026-04-15; `qwen3-coder-plus` is stale |\n     | agent 0.26.11 | opencode/minimax-m2.5-free | our default `nemotron-3-super-free` is deprecated in the models.dev snapshot; kilo IDs are dead |\n     | OpenCode 1.18.34 | big-pickle | free models: big-pickle, exo-free, fledge-alpha-free, ling-3.0-flash-fin-free, ling-3.1-flash-free, longcat-2.5-preview-free, mimo-v2.6-flash-free, muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free, nemotron-3-ultra-free, nemotron-3.5-lightning-free, space-bunny-free; grok-code and the claude-3 IDs are obsolete |\n\n     These other-tool catalogue updates have not been applied yet; at minimum, document them in the case study.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Created `src/models/aliases.mjs`.** Its full contents are described above. Patterns:\n     - `CODEX_FAMILY_MODEL_PATTERN = /^gpt-(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)*)-([a-z]+)$/`\n     - `CODEX_LATEST_MODEL_PATTERN = /^gpt-([a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:-[a-z][a-z0-9]*)*)-latest$/`\n     - `CLAUDE_FAMILY_MODEL_PATTERN = /^claude-([a-z]+)-(\\d+(?:-\\d+)?)$/`\n\n     The runtime registry is a Map of tool → Map(lowercased alias → id).\n   - **Modified `src/models/catalog.mjs`:**\n     - Imports `deriveClaudeFamilyAliases` and `deriveCodexFamilyAliases` from './aliases.mjs'.\n     - `explicitClaudeModels` holds the static Claude entries. Then:\n       `claudeModels = {...explicitClaudeModels, ...derived aliases not already in explicit}`.\n     - New exports: `currentCodexModels`, `HIDDEN_CODEX_MODEL_IDS`, `legacyCodexModels`, `LEGACY_CLAUDE_MODEL_ALIASES`, `CODEX_FAMILY_ALIASES`.\n     - `getCodexModelVariants` builds `{...CODEX_FAMILY_ALIASES, ...codexModels}` plus openai/ and openai. variants of every bare model and alias.\n     - `MODELS_SUPPORTING_1M_CONTEXT` gained claude-sonnet-5-5, sonnet-5-5, mythos and best.\n     - `CLAUDE_MODELS` gained claude-sonnet-5-5.\n   - **Modified `src/models/index.mjs`** (was 1100 lines; the limit check warns at 1350):\n     - **Imports and re-exports:** imports `CODEX_FAMILY_ALIASES`, `HIDDEN_CODEX_MODEL_IDS`, `LEGACY_CLAUDE_MODEL_ALIASES` and `legacyCodexModels`. Imports `deriveClaudeFamilyAliases`, `deriveCodexFamilyAliases`, `getRuntimeModelAlias`, `listClaudeFamilies` and `registerRuntimeModelAlias` from aliases, and re-exports `clearRuntimeModelAliases`, the derive functions, `getRuntimeModelAlias` and `registerRuntimeModelAlias`.\n     - **Codex catalogue and cache:** new `getInstalledCodexModelCatalogue()` returns `[{slug, visibility}]` with a TTL cache (`parsedCodexModelsCacheTtl`, `CODEX_MODELS_CACHE_TTL_MS`). `getInstalledCodexModels()` now derives from it.\n     - **`mapModelForTool`:** checks `getRuntimeModelAlias(tool, model)` first.\n     - **`primaryModelNames`:**\n       - codex: `['sol','astra','luna','terra','gpt-6.1-sol','gpt-6-astra','gpt-6-sol','gpt-6-luna','gpt-5.6-sol','gpt-5.6-terra','gpt-5.6-luna','gpt-5.5', FORMAL_AI]`\n       - claude: adds 'mythos' and 'best'.\n     - **Listing filter:** `CODEX_UNLISTED_MODEL_NAMES` and `isListedModelName(tool, key, modelId)`:\n       - codex excludes `openai[/.]` keys, legacy and hidden models, and aliases that point at them;\n       - claude excludes dotted keys `/\\d\\.\\d/` and legacy aliases.\n\n       This is applied in `getAvailableModelNames`.\n     - **Error message:** `validateModelName`'s message-building code was extracted into `buildUnrecognizedModelResult(model, tool, shortNames)`.\n     - **New runtime-validation helpers:**\n       - `OPENAI_MODEL_PREFIX_PATTERN`, `CLAUDE_FAMILY_SHORTHAND_PATTERN = /^([a-z]+)-(\\d+(?:[-.]\\d+)?)$/`\n       - `isLiveFamilyAliasCandidate`, `resolveLiveFamilyAlias`, `expandClaudeFamilyShorthand`\n       - `loadRuntimeModels(toolName, options)` returns `{models, hidden}`.\n       - `listRuntimeModelNames`, `withInstalledCatalogueWarning`\n     - **Rewritten `validateRuntimeModelName`:**\n       - If static validation is valid and the input is not a family alias candidate (or carries `[1m]`), return 'bundled'.\n       - Otherwise load live models, then try in order: live alias (register it, source 'live-alias'), static, exact live match, Claude shorthand expansion (register it, source 'provider'), provider pass-through.\n       - Otherwise return an error that lists live models for codex.\n     - **Logging:** `validateAndExitOnInvalidModel` logs `result.warning` at level 'warning'.\n     - **Fallbacks:**\n       - claude 'claude-sonnet-5-5' → 'sonnet-5'\n       - codex 'gpt-6.1-sol' → 'gpt-6-sol' (and the openai. variant)\n       - 'gpt-6-astra' → 'gpt-6.1-sol' (and the openai. variant)\n   - **Modified `src/codex.options.lib.mjs`:** imports `getRuntimeModelAlias` from './models/aliases.mjs'. Now:\n     `mapModelToId = model => getRuntimeModelAlias('codex', model) || CODEX_MODEL_VARIANTS[model] || model`\n   - **Modified `src/claude.model-utils.lib.mjs`:** imports `getRuntimeModelAlias` from './models/index.mjs'. Adds:\n     `mapBaseModel = model => getRuntimeModelAlias('claude', model) || availableModels[model] || model`\n     It is used for both the plain path and the `[1m]` path. The rolling-alias preservation check still runs first.\n   - **Created `tests/test-issue-2591-latest-model-aliases.mjs`** (`@hive-mind-test-suite default`, 15 tests, all passing). It covers:\n     - astra\n     - each family resolving to its newest version\n     - a live new family (gpt-7-nova → nova)\n     - a live newer Sol (gpt-6.2-sol, including openai/sol)\n     - listing filtering\n     - legacy models still accepted\n     - typo listing built from live data\n     - the warning\n     - Claude aliases (opus-5-5, sonnet-5-5, best), mythos, dotted aliases, 1M support\n     - opus-6 pass-through\n     - live mythos-6\n     - Claude listing filtering\n     - fallbacks\n\n     It uses `CODEX_0_160_MODELS` and calls `clearRuntimeModelAliases()` before each test.\n   - **Created `experiments/issue-2591-print-model-listings.mjs`:** prints listings for each tool and the validation results for sample inputs.\n   - **Created `docs/case-studies/issue-2591/data/reproduction/`:**\n     - `before-fix-listings.txt`: the old code shows 62 Codex models and astra → \"Did you mean terra\", reproducing the screenshot.\n     - `after-fix-listings.txt`: 13 Codex models.\n   - **Existing data** from before this session: the `github/`, `codex/`, `claude/` and `cli-model-catalogues/` directories under the case study, plus `experiments/issue-2591-extract-claude-code-aliases.mjs`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`node -e` import of `index.mjs` failed:** use-m bootstrap `createRequire` raised ERR_INVALID_ARG_VALUE '[eval]'. Fixed by running code from a script file in experiments/ instead.\n   - **Cumbersome TTL expression:** simplified to a `Number.parseInt` check.\n   - **Earlier problems** (from before this session):\n     - `pkill -f` killed the shell; avoid it.\n     - `npm ci --ignore-scripts` was needed to install semver.\n     - `file` and `jq` are not available.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Root causes:**\n     - Issue #2043's complete-trio rule (GPT-6 has no Terra), so `sol` and `luna` were stale and `astra` had no alias.\n     - Static bundled catalogue only, with no family aliases derived from the live catalogue.\n     - The listing included openai variants and obsolete models.\n     - The Claude catalogue lagged Claude Code (sonnet-5-5, mythos, best).\n   - **Verified against the real codex binary:**\n     - runtime `astra`, `sol`, `luna` and `terra` resolve with source 'live-alias';\n     - `astar` suggests \"astra\" and lists only 13 models.\n\n   **Current test failures to fix** (out of the 30 model tests listed in /tmp/model-tests.txt):\n   - **Pinned old Claude mappings.** These tests expect opus → claude-opus-5, sonnet → claude-sonnet-5, or `[1m]` variants of those; update them to claude-opus-5-5 and claude-sonnet-5-5:\n     - test-fable-5-model-support\n     - test-issue-1978-sub-agent-model\n     - test-opus-46-model-support (\"Should map to claude-opus-5[1m]\")\n     - test-issue-882-fixes\n     - test-sonnet-46, test-opus-47, test-opus-5 and test-sonnet-5 model-support\n     - test-opus-48-model-support\n     - test-opusplan-support: was already failing on main because it expects opus → claude-opus-4-6; fix it too.\n   - **Fallbacks:** the opus fallback is now 'opus-5', where tests expected 'opus-4-8', because opus maps to claude-opus-5-5 and its fallback is 'opus-5'. Affects test-codex-support (\"Claude default fallback model resolves from opus to opus-4-8\") and test-issue-1949-overload-no-model-switch (\"switches opus -> fallback\"). Update the expectations to opus-5.\n   - **test-codex-support:** the primaryModelNames deepEqual needs to expect the new codex list.\n   - **test-issue-2202-new-model-support:** the gpt-6-astra and openai.gpt-6-astra fallbacks are now gpt-6.1-sol and openai.gpt-6.1-sol.\n   - **test-issue-2043-codex-model-aliases:** the `generationAliases` expectations must become sol: gpt-6.1-sol, terra: gpt-5.6-terra, luna: gpt-6-luna. Add a comment about the per-family change in #2591.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The only user message: \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind