    "content": [
      {
        "tool_use_id": "toolu_017JnxxXEJvepCyECDLB1wx8",
        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "242\tCLOSED\topencode/qwen3.6-plus-free is no longer available, set opencode/nemotron-3-super-free as default model\tbug, documentation, enhancement\t2026-04-10T16:19:13Z\n327\tOPEN\topencode/nemotron-3-super-free is no longer served by OpenCode Zen; update free models and the default compaction cascade\t\t2026-10-02T16:21:12Z\n164\tOPEN\tUse https://github.com/link-foundation/set-process-name instead of our own implementation\tdocumentation, enhancement\t2026-02-13T22:46:53Z\n6\tOPEN\tTry to restore models and models-macro workflow\tenhancement\t2025-11-20T10:13:26Z\n1\tOPEN\tMaximum safety architecture\tdocumentation, enhancement\t2025-12-01T10:22:36Z\n# Case Study — Issue #2043: Future-proof Codex model aliases and OpenAI prefixes\n\n- **Issue:** [link-assistant/hive-mind#2043](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2043)\n- **Pull request:** [#2044](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2044)\n- **Investigated:** 2026-07-11\n- **Affected command:** `solve --tool codex --model <model>` and the Telegram `/codex` alias\n\n## Executive summary\n\nHive Mind already listed `gpt-5.6-sol`, `gpt-5.6-terra`, and `gpt-5.6-luna`, but\nrejected the intended short forms `sol`, `terra`, and `luna`. It also accepted\nonly a hand-maintained subset of `openai.` model names and accepted no\n`openai/` forms for Codex. The issue screenshot captures all three short names\nfailing validation before Codex starts.\n\nThe root cause was duplicated, manually enumerated model data. Mapping,\nvalidation, compatibility, and error-message lists were based on static object\nkeys. Each new OpenAI model therefore needed every prefix spelling to be added\nindividually, while generation-relative aliases had no representation at all.\n\nThe solution derives one Codex model-variant map from the canonical catalog:\n\n1. `sol`, `terra`, and `luna` resolve to the newest generation for which all\n   three tiers exist.\n2. Both `openai/` and `openai.` forms are generated for every known Codex/OpenAI\n   model and for the three short aliases.\n3. Mapping, validation, compatibility checks, and valid-model output consume the\n   same generated map.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nBefore the fix, each of these was rejected as an unrecognized Codex model:\n\n```text\n/codex https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/1 --model sol\n/codex https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/1 --model terra\n/codex https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/1 --model luna\n```\n\nThe screenshot's available-model list exposed the inconsistency: full",
        "is_error": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "parent_tool_use_id": null,
  "session_id": "41cebf9b-7516-44c0-8422-5bbafe26cee9",
  "uuid": "402f9b10-1899-4e05-84fa-c1165fe3e619",
  "timestamp": "2026-10-07T09:33:55.664Z",
  "tool_use_result": {
    "stdout": "242\tCLOSED\topencode/qwen3.6-plus-free is no longer available, set opencode/nemotron-3-super-free as default model\tbug, documentation, enhancement\t2026-04-10T16:19:13Z\n327\tOPEN\topencode/nemotron-3-super-free is no longer served by OpenCode Zen; update free models and the default compaction cascade\t\t2026-10-02T16:21:12Z\n164\tOPEN\tUse https://github.com/link-foundation/set-process-name instead of our own implementation\tdocumentation, enhancement\t2026-02-13T22:46:53Z\n6\tOPEN\tTry to restore models and models-macro workflow\tenhancement\t2025-11-20T10:13:26Z\n1\tOPEN\tMaximum safety architecture\tdocumentation, enhancement\t2025-12-01T10:22:36Z\n# Case Study — Issue #2043: Future-proof Codex model aliases and OpenAI prefixes\n\n- **Issue:** [link-assistant/hive-mind#2043](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2043)\n- **Pull request:** [#2044](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2044)\n- **Investigated:** 2026-07-11\n- **Affected command:** `solve --tool codex --model <model>` and the Telegram `/codex` alias\n\n## Executive summary\n\nHive Mind already listed `gpt-5.6-sol`, `gpt-5.6-terra`, and `gpt-5.6-luna`, but\nrejected the intended short forms `sol`, `terra`, and `luna`. It also accepted\nonly a hand-maintained subset of `openai.` model names and accepted no\n`openai/` forms for Codex. The issue screenshot captures all three short names\nfailing validation before Codex starts.\n\nThe root cause was duplicated, manually enumerated model data. Mapping,\nvalidation, compatibility, and error-message lists were based on static object\nkeys. Each new OpenAI model therefore needed every prefix spelling to be added\nindividually, while generation-relative aliases had no representation at all.\n\nThe solution derives one Codex model-variant map from the canonical catalog:\n\n1. `sol`, `terra`, and `luna` resolve to the newest generation for which all\n   three tiers exist.\n2. Both `openai/` and `openai.` forms are generated for every known Codex/OpenAI\n   model and for the three short aliases.\n3. Mapping, validation, compatibility checks, and valid-model output consume the\n   same generated map.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nBefore the fix, each of these was rejected as an unrecognized Codex model:\n\n```text\n/codex https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/1 --model sol\n/codex https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/1 --model terra\n/codex https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/1 --model luna\n```\n\nThe screenshot's available-model list exposed the inconsistency: full",
    "stderr": "",
    "interrupted": false,
    "isImage": false,
    "noOutputExpected": false
  }
}
