{
  "type": "user",
  "message": {
    "role": "user",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Solve GitHub issue https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591, \"We must support all obvious aliases for latest versions of models\". Work in /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791364120785, only on branch `issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2`, and update the existing PR #2592; do not create a new PR.\n\n   What the issue asks for:\n   - **astra alias:** `astra` must resolve to the latest gpt-6-astra. The screenshot shows `/codex --model astra` failing with \"Did you mean terra\".\n   - **Dynamic aliases:** derive aliases from new model names without code changes.\n   - **Full support:** support all available models to their full potential.\n   - **Real listings:** the \"Available models\" list must be the real current catalogue of codex, claude and the other CLIs, with no obsolete entries.\n   - **Case study:** collect data in `./docs/case-studies/issue-2591` and write a deep case study covering timeline, requirements, root causes, solutions, existing libraries and online research.\n   - **Debug output:** add debug output if it is needed.\n   - **Upstream reports:** report issues to other repositories, with reproductions, workarounds and suggested fixes.\n   - **Apply everywhere:** fix the problem in every place it occurs in the codebase.\n   - **One PR:** do all of this in a single PR.\n\n   Standard solver guidelines:\n   - Write tests first.\n   - Keep scripts in experiments/ and examples/.\n   - Make atomic commits.\n   - Run lint, prettier and the tests before pushing.\n   - Add a changeset.\n   - Update the PR with `gh pr edit 2592`, then run `gh pr ready 2592`.\n   - Check CI.\n   - Do not remove existing features.\n\n   Constraints:\n   - Never send the user's email to external services.\n   - Push only to issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Leaf module `src/models/aliases.mjs`:**\n     - `deriveCodexFamilyAliases`: pattern `^gpt-(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)*)-([a-z]+)$`, each family resolving to its own newest version. `gpt-<name>-latest` gives the alias `<name>`.\n     - `deriveClaudeFamilyAliases`: pattern `^claude-([a-z]+)-(\\d+(?:-\\d+)?)$`. Produces `family-ver`, the dotted forms, `claude-family-5.5`, and `family` → newest.\n     - Also exports `listClaudeFamilies`, `deriveFamilyAliasesForTool` and `compareNumericVersions`.\n     - Runtime registry: `registerRuntimeModelAlias`, `getRuntimeModelAlias`, `clearRuntimeModelAliases`.\n   - **Codex catalogue (codex-cli 0.160.0):**\n     - `currentCodexModels`, `HIDDEN_CODEX_MODEL_IDS`, `legacyCodexModels`.\n     - `CODEX_FAMILY_ALIASES` = {astra: gpt-6-astra, sol: gpt-6.1-sol, luna: gpt-6-luna, terra: gpt-5.6-terra, daybreak-blue, daybreak-red}.\n     - The listing filter `isListedModelName` hides openai-prefixed, legacy and hidden models; for claude it hides dotted keys and the legacy haiku-3 / haiku-3-5.\n   - **Claude:** opus → claude-opus-5-5 and sonnet → claude-sonnet-5-5, matching Claude Code 2.1.292. Adds `best` → claude-fable-5-1, `mythos` and `sonnet-5-5`.\n   - **Runtime validation:** `validateRuntimeModelName` returns these sources:\n     - 'live-alias' when the alias resolves against `codex debug models` (cached for 1h; override with `HIVE_MIND_CODEX_MODELS_CACHE_TTL_MS`);\n     - 'provider' for Claude shorthand expansion (opus-6 → claude-opus-6) and for pass-through;\n     - a warning when the model is not in the installed catalogue;\n     - an error message listing the live models.\n   - **Fallbacks:** claude-sonnet-5-5 → sonnet-5, gpt-6.1-sol → gpt-6-sol, gpt-6-astra → gpt-6.1-sol. The opus fallback is now opus-5 and the sonnet fallback sonnet-5.\n   - **Gemini:** `flash`, `pro`, `flash-lite` and `auto` now pass through as Gemini CLI's own rolling aliases. Gemini CLI 0.62.0 resolves flash to gemini-3-flash-preview, 3.8-flash or 3.5-flash, and no longer lists 2.5-flash.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`src/models/aliases.mjs`** (created, 145 lines; prettier applied): described above.\n   - **`src/models/catalog.mjs`** (modified):\n     - Earlier changes: explicit and derived Claude aliases, the codex catalogue split, `CODEX_MODELS = {...CODEX_MODEL_VARIANTS}`.\n     - This session, `geminiModels` was rewritten:\n       - Rolling aliases: auto→'auto', gemini→'flash', flash→'flash', pro→'pro', lite→'flash-lite', 'flash-lite'→'flash-lite', gemini-flash→'flash', gemini-pro→'pro'.\n       - Version shorthands: '3-flash', '3-pro', '3.1-pro', '3.5-flash', '3.8-flash', '3.1-flash-lite', '3.5-flash-lite'.\n       - Full IDs: gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-3.5-flash-lite, gemini-3.1-flash-lite, gemini-3.1-pro-preview, gemini-3-flash-preview, gemini-3-pro-preview.\n       - Gemini 2.5 entries are kept and commented \"still accepted for pinned configurations\".\n     - `qwenModels` gained 'coder-model', 'qwen3.7-plus', 'qwen3.7-max', 'qwen3.8-max', 'qwen3.8-flash' and 'qwen3-coder-next'. An accidental duplicate in QWEN_MODELS was removed.\n     - Defaults are unchanged: agent 'nemotron-3-super-free', qwen 'qwen3-coder-plus', gemini 'flash', codex 'gpt-6-sol', claude 'opus'.\n   - **`src/models/index.mjs`** (1239 lines): the earlier changes, as in the previous summary.\n     - `mapModelForTool` checks `getRuntimeModelAlias` first.\n     - `primaryModelNames.codex` = ['sol','astra','luna','terra','gpt-6.1-sol','gpt-6-astra','gpt-6-sol','gpt-6-luna','gpt-5.6-sol','gpt-5.6-terra','gpt-5.6-luna','gpt-5.5', FORMAL_AI]\n     - Also contains `isListedModelName`, `buildUnrecognizedModelResult`, the runtime helpers, and the rewritten `validateRuntimeModelName`.\n   - **`src/model-reasoning.lib.mjs`** (modified this session): imports `getRuntimeModelAlias` from './models/aliases.mjs' and adds:\n     ```js\n     // Live family aliases (issue #2591) resolve to whatever validation recorded.\n     const resolveCodexModelId = model => getRuntimeModelAlias('codex', model) ?? CODEX_MODEL_VARIANTS[model] ?? model;\n     ```\n     This is used in `getBundledReasoningCapabilities` and `getModelReasoningCapabilities`.\n   - **`src/codex.options.lib.mjs`:** `mapModelToId = model => getRuntimeModelAlias('codex', model) || CODEX_MODEL_VARIANTS[model] || model`.\n   - **`src/claude.model-utils.lib.mjs`:** `mapBaseModel` uses the runtime alias.\n   - **`tests/test-issue-2591-latest-model-aliases.mjs`** (17 tests, all pass). Added this session:\n     - reasoning capabilities for the live alias `nova`, using catalogue `{sources:[{id:'codex-cli',status:'ok',models:[{id:'gpt-7-nova',supportedReasoningEfforts:['low','high']}]}]}`;\n     - \"Gemini rolling aliases are left to the installed Gemini CLI\";\n     - \"Qwen Code's own default model is accepted\".\n   - **Tests updated this session to the new expectations:**\n     - test-sonnet-46, test-opus-46, test-opus-47, test-opus-48, test-opus-5 and test-sonnet-5 (model-support)\n     - test-fable-5-model-support, test-issue-1978-sub-agent-model, test-issue-882-fixes, test-opusplan-support\n     - test-codex-support: primaryModelNames and the opus → opus-5 fallback\n     - test-issue-1949-overload-no-model-switch: fallbackModel is now 'opus-5'\n     - test-issue-2043-codex-model-aliases: sol gpt-6.1-sol, terra gpt-5.6-terra, luna gpt-6-luna, with an issue #2591 comment\n     - test-issue-2202-new-model-support: astra fallback is gpt-6.1-sol, and opus/sonnet map to the 5-5 models\n     - test-gemini-support: flash, pro and flash-lite resolve to themselves; the command includes '--model flash'\n   - **`experiments/`:**\n     - `issue-2591-print-model-listings.mjs` and `issue-2591-extract-claude-code-aliases.mjs`;\n     - new: `issue-2591-other-tools-validation.mjs`, which showed qwen `coder-model` rejected and agent `nemotron-3.5-lightning-free` rejected before the fix; the other tools pass new IDs through to the provider.\n   - **`docs/case-studies/issue-2591/data/`:**\n     - `github/`: issue JSON, screenshot, PR comments. The first solve attempt failed at 2026-10-07T07:18 with \"File not found: …/e.g\".\n     - `codex/`: the 0.160.0 debug models JSON and its summary.\n     - `claude/`: the Claude Code 2.1.292 aliases.\n     - `cli-model-catalogues/`: gemini 0.62.0, qwen 0.24.7, agent 0.26.11, opencode 1.18.34.\n     - `reproduction/before-fix-listings.txt` (62 codex models, astra → terra) and `after-fix-listings.txt` (13 codex models).\n     - Not yet committed.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **sed with line addresses misplaced a comment** in test-codex-support. Fixed with a python string replace.\n   - **A python replace hit both qwenModels and QWEN_MODELS.** Removed the duplicate from QWEN_MODELS.\n   - **eslint errors in experiments/** ('console'/'process' not defined). These files are outside the npm lint globs, so they were ignored.\n   - **Prettier warnings in aliases.mjs.** Fixed with `prettier --write`.\n   - **From the earlier session:**\n     - a `node -e` import of index.mjs fails, so use script files instead;\n     - avoid `pkill -f`;\n     - `file` and `jq` are unavailable.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Root causes:**\n     - The complete-trio rule from issue #2043 (GPT-6 has no Terra) left sol and luna stale and gave astra no alias.\n     - The catalogue was static only.\n     - The listing included openai variants and obsolete models.\n     - The Claude catalogue lagged Claude Code.\n     - The Gemini aliases were pinned to stale 2.5 models.\n     - Qwen Code's default `coder-model` was rejected.\n   - **Upstream:** link-assistant/agent#327 (OPEN) already reports that nemotron-3-super-free is no longer served; Hive Mind is waiting for Agent to name a replacement. Kilo IDs (z-ai/glm-5:free and others) are missing from the models.dev snapshot; this could be added as a comment on agent#327.\n   - **Other tools:** the agent and opencode defaults and catalogues were not changed; document them as follow-ups in the case study.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The only user message: \"Issue to solve: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2591 / Your prepared branch: issue-2591-1b69dfe657e2 / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1791364120785 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/pull/2592 / Pull request description was edited after last commit / Merge status is UNKNOWN / Continue.\"\n   - System nudges asked for brief status updates.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Check the background `npm test` (output in /tmp/npm-test.log; it started before the gemini and qwen changes). Rerun any failing tests, especially gemini-, qwen- and model-info-related ones such as tests/model-info.test.mjs and test-formal-ai-*.\n   - Commit the case-study data and experiments.\n   - Write `docs/case-studies/issue-2591/README.md`, covering timeline, requirements, root causes, solutions, libraries and online facts. Include the other-CLI findings, the gemini and qwen changes, and agent#327.\n   - Optionally update `docs/case-studies/issue-2043/README.md` with a note that issue #2591 supersedes the complete-trio rule.\n   - Optionally comment on link-assistant/agent#327 with the missing Kilo IDs evidence.\n   - Add a changeset in `.changeset/`.\n   - Run lint, `format:check` and `bash scripts/check-file-line-limits.sh`.\n   - Push the branch; it includes the unpushed merge 9065118d and commit 5103bbe9.\n   - Update the PR #2592 title and description (reproduction, tests, before/after listings).\n   - Check CI, then run `gh pr ready 2592`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just committed 5103bbe9, \"fix(models): derive latest-version family aliases and list only current models (#2591)\". It includes all src and tests changes:\n   - the aliases module, catalogue and index;\n   - codex options, claude model utils and model-reasoning;\n   - the gemini and qwen catalogue changes;\n   - the updated tests and the new 17-test file.\n\n 