        "type": "tool_result",
        "content": "Web search results for query: \"Codex CLI \"codex debug models\" model catalogue visibility\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Codex CLI Model Catalogue Architecture: Providers, Discovery, and Debugging Model Resolution\",\"url\":\"https://codex.danielvaughan.com/2026/05/04/codex-cli-model-catalogue-architecture-providers-discovery-debug/\"},{\"title\":\"codex cli\",\"url\":\"https://explyt.ai/docs/explyt/connect/codex-cli\"},{\"title\":\"model discovery\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openclaw.ai/plugins/codex-harness-reference/model-discovery.md\"},{\"title\":\"> ## Documentation Index\",\"url\":\"https://openrouter.helicone.ai/docs/cookbook/coding-agents/codex-cli.md\"},{\"title\":\"DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/owen_fox/codex-desktop-not-showing-custom-models-5-fixes-2026-10b2\"},{\"title\":\"codex cli\",\"url\":\"https://docs.digitalocean.com/products/marketplace/catalog/codex-cli/\"},{\"title\":\"> ## Documentation Index\",\"url\":\"https://2.26.113.50.sslip.io/docs/cookbook/coding-agents/codex-cli.md\"},{\"title\":\"> ## Documentation Index\",\"url\":\"https://orouter.159.195.193.23.sslip.io/docs/cookbook/coding-agents/codex-cli.md\"},{\"title\":\"model discovery\",\"url\":\"https://docs2.openclaw.ai/plugins/codex-harness-reference/model-discovery\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about Codex CLI and model catalogue visibility. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Model Catalogue Architecture\n\nCodex CLI uses a model catalogue—a layered system that merges bundled metadata, remote refreshes, custom JSON overrides, and per-provider discovery into a single runtime view—to resolve which model to use and what capabilities that model supports.\n\n## Debugging Model Visibility Issues\n\nWhen Codex starts, the app-server reads all three layers, resolves them, and exposes the result through an internal model/list endpoint, which the CLI renders directly so custom models show up.\n\nA common issue affecting model visibility is a cache file at ~/.codex/models_cache.json that may not resync after you switch providers or edit a catalog, potentially keeping an old or empty list showing even when your config is correct. Deleting that file forces a clean rebuild on the next launch.\n\n## Model Visibility Control\n\nIn model catalogue configurations, models include a \"visibility\" field (e.g., set to \"list\") that controls whether they appear in discovery and selection interfaces.\n\nFor more detailed debugging and understanding of how `codex debug models` specifically handles model catalogue visibility, the first search result from Daniel Vaughan's comprehensive guide on Codex CLI Model Catalogue Architecture appears to be the most authoritative technical resource on this topic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
      }
    ]
  },
